{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSW6Ztu6T2Ne6BQeM8Kq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me summarize my analysis findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment entity: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14`\n- ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED: `Shipment.kt:23-27`\n- Repository methods (save, findById, existsById): `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-22`\n- Controller with create, getById, list endpoints: `ShipmentController.kt:26-55`\n- Error handling uses ApiException subclasses with status codes: `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24`\n- Error codes enum: `ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- Global exception handler converts exceptions to ApiError envelope: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28`\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses rather than building error responses\n2. ResourceNotFoundException → 404 (used for missing resources)\n3. ConflictException → 409 (used for state/constraint conflicts)\n4. Each exception carries an ErrorCode enum value\n5. Tests use MockMvc with status() and jsonPath() assertions\n6. Tests verify both status AND error envelope body for failures\n7. Repository uses in-memory ConcurrentHashMap for storage\n8. Success responses return domain objects directly or with ResponseEntity.status()\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Must add the confirm endpoint method\n2. `ApiError.kt` - Must add new ErrorCode for shipment state conflict (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Must add comprehensive tests for all confirm scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Idempotency: Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment must succeed without throwing\n2. State validation: Cannot transition from CANCELLED to CONFIRMED\n3. Missing shipment: Must return 404, not 500\n4. Concurrent modifications: Repository uses ConcurrentHashMap but update isn't atomic across read+write\n\n**Open questions:** None - the requirement clearly defines all four cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED idempotent, CANCELLED→error, missing→404).\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`** - Add one new ErrorCode enum value: `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to represent state conflicts when trying to confirm a cancelled shipment.\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`** - Add a new POST endpoint method `confirm`:\n   - Path: `/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n   - Logic: Find shipment by ID, throw ResourceNotFoundException if missing\n   - If shipment status is CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - If shipment status is CREATED: update to CONFIRMED\n   - If shipment status is CONFIRMED: do nothing (idempotent)\n   - Return the shipment with ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.OK)\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** - Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment moves it to CONFIRMED status`\n   - `confirms an already confirmed shipment succeeds without changing it`\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409`\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404`\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:**\n\nI considered using an existing error code (e.g., reusing SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS), but rejected this because:\n- Error codes are part of the API contract and should be precise\n- SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS specifically means duplicate creation\n- A dedicated SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code is clearer for clients to handle\n- The ApiError.kt file explicitly notes \"add one deliberately\", indicating this is the right approach\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Scenario | Input | Process | Output | HTTP Status |\n|----------|-------|---------|--------|-------------|\n| Confirm CREATED shipment | shipmentId=S-1, status=CREATED | Read shipment, update status to CONFIRMED, save | Shipment object with CONFIRMED status | 200 |\n| Retry confirm CONFIRMED | shipmentId=S-1, status=CONFIRMED | Read shipment, no update needed | Shipment object with CONFIRMED status | 200 |\n| Confirm CANCELLED shipment | shipmentId=S-1, status=CANCELLED | Read shipment, throw ConflictException | ApiError envelope with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE | 409 |\n| Confirm non-existent | shipmentId=missing | findById returns null, throw ResourceNotFoundException | ApiError envelope with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test 1: Happy path (CREATED→CONFIRMED)** - Create a shipment, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED and response contains updated shipment\n2. **Test 2: Idempotent retry (CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED)** - Create and confirm a shipment, confirm it again, verify no error and status remains CONFIRMED\n3. **Test 3: Reject CANCELLED** - Create a shipment, manually set it to CANCELLED in repository, attempt confirm, verify 409 response with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code\n4. **Test 4: Not found** - Attempt to confirm non-existent shipment, verify 404 response with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1827,"cache_read_input_tokens":16930,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1827},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef8464d1-80ef-46d1-970d-9fe8bdc281aa","uuid":"1476e236-a7ea-4e39-b0fb-bf520b2f84d4","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:12:16.944Z","request_id":"req_011CfSW6ZU7LCbe5twtDZfet"}
